WEBVTT

00:01:47.120 --> 00:01:49.110
Death day, huh?

00:02:51.630 --> 00:02:54.160
It's still light outside.

00:02:54.160 --> 00:02:55.320
Why did you...

00:02:55.320 --> 00:02:57.760
I want you to get back the death day.

00:02:58.390 --> 00:03:00.930
You'll be rewarded handsomely.

00:03:00.930 --> 00:03:02.770
All you have to do

00:03:03.380 --> 00:03:06.150
is get back my death day.

00:03:22.030 --> 00:03:23.050
Shitoto.

00:03:23.050 --> 00:03:27.420
A fortune teller who can foretell a client's death day.

00:03:27.420 --> 00:03:29.420
That's quite something.

00:03:29.420 --> 00:03:33.150
I didn't want to know something like that.

00:03:33.150 --> 00:03:36.400
He came to me of his own volition.

00:03:36.400 --> 00:03:38.570
I don't believe in fortunetelling.

00:03:39.020 --> 00:03:43.430
But when he told you that he knew when your death day is, you suddenly grew curious.

00:03:43.430 --> 00:03:46.710
Yes, I partially believed him.

00:03:46.710 --> 00:03:48.940
It was a foolish curiosity.

00:03:48.940 --> 00:03:54.950
But as the predicted date of my death grew closer, I...

00:03:55.570 --> 00:03:59.110
Jigen Daisuke, if my death comes to pass,

00:03:59.110 --> 00:04:03.520
I want you to destroy the lithograph that Shitoto values more than his own life,

00:04:03.520 --> 00:04:06.460
and end his career as a fortune teller.

00:04:07.040 --> 00:04:09.900
I know this doesn't seem to make sense.

00:04:09.900 --> 00:04:16.180
But it will serve as my revenge on the one who ruined the last years of my life

00:04:16.180 --> 00:04:18.470
by tainting them with the fear of death.

00:04:19.660 --> 00:04:20.620
Hey!

00:04:20.620 --> 00:04:21.760
Are you saying today is...

00:04:21.760 --> 00:04:23.640
I'm counting on you,

00:04:24.270 --> 00:04:25.770
assassin!

00:04:30.760 --> 00:04:34.030
There was a man who wanted to know when he would meet his end.

00:04:34.830 --> 00:04:40.000
And once he knew his death day, he wished he had never known it.

00:04:40.000 --> 00:04:41.940
So full of himself, right?

00:04:41.940 --> 00:04:45.250
And he did in fact die on his death day.

00:04:47.230 --> 00:04:50.130
A fortune teller that foretells the day you'll die.

00:04:50.130 --> 00:04:52.730
Does such a person really exist?

00:04:53.810 --> 00:04:57.220
I have confirmed eleven mysterious and unrelated

00:04:57.220 --> 00:04:59.910
murder cases and accidental deaths.

00:04:59.910 --> 00:05:01.550
Unrelated?

00:05:01.550 --> 00:05:04.220
Then how exactly are they
connected as one overall case?

00:05:04.220 --> 00:05:09.730
All those who died in those murder cases and accidents were victims of Lupin.

00:05:10.730 --> 00:05:13.470
Furthermore, although their ages and the ways they died were different,

00:05:13.470 --> 00:05:17.710
there is someone with a
direct connection with all of them.

00:05:18.310 --> 00:05:22.210
The fortune teller who predicts people's death day, Shitoto Chandler.

00:05:22.630 --> 00:05:26.750
Without a doubt, they all met with this fortune teller.

00:05:27.960 --> 00:05:32.720
I believe we can gather intel on Lupin from this man.

00:05:34.380 --> 00:05:36.680
I'd rather not pull the trigger if I don't have to.

00:05:37.180 --> 00:05:39.600
You aren't my target.

00:05:40.130 --> 00:05:42.930
Where is the lithograph you use
to determine the death days?

00:05:42.930 --> 00:05:46.160
I don't foretell the day of death.

00:05:46.160 --> 00:05:49.180
I am interested in my client's entire life.

00:05:49.180 --> 00:05:53.910
That person's past, future and their final moments.

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:01.450
What's that?

00:06:01.450 --> 00:06:05.920
The lithograph has already lost its power due to being set on fire.

00:06:05.920 --> 00:06:09.290
So someone else got to it first?

00:06:09.980 --> 00:06:13.720
This means you can't do your job anymore, right?

00:06:13.720 --> 00:06:17.150
There is a right time for everything.

00:06:17.150 --> 00:06:19.690
You give up awfully easily.

00:06:25.830 --> 00:06:27.070
They're fast!

00:06:27.070 --> 00:06:29.560
This is the police. Come out quietly.

00:06:29.560 --> 00:06:31.100
You're under arrest!

00:07:01.350 --> 00:07:03.700
Assistant Inspector... this isn't Lupin!

00:07:03.700 --> 00:07:06.180
Lupin? What kind of joke is that?

00:07:06.180 --> 00:07:08.470
It may be one of his disguises.

00:07:08.470 --> 00:07:09.430
Don't let him fool you.

00:07:09.430 --> 00:07:12.910
Don't be stupid.
The name I got from my parents is Jigen Dai—

00:08:36.480 --> 00:08:37.850
Do you have some smokes?

00:08:39.550 --> 00:08:40.850
Gitanes?

00:08:42.110 --> 00:08:43.730
I don't like these.

00:08:44.890 --> 00:08:47.740
Don't be so picky. I just saved you.

00:09:07.380 --> 00:09:10.450
I shall grant you wealth and fame.

00:09:18.320 --> 00:09:22.440
You just need to predict the day of death of the Third's victims.

00:09:24.070 --> 00:09:27.410
On the day you've determined as their death day,

00:09:27.410 --> 00:09:30.520
they will certainly die.

00:09:48.300 --> 00:09:52.990
Leave it to me. The stage is already prepared.

00:10:01.830 --> 00:10:03.030
Yummy!

00:10:03.030 --> 00:10:05.150
Home-cooked food, by you?

00:10:05.810 --> 00:10:07.400
It's Grandma's recipe.

00:10:07.400 --> 00:10:10.940
Oh? I remember seeing a guy like you

00:10:10.940 --> 00:10:13.180
in a movie I watched recently.

00:10:15.030 --> 00:10:18.580
He was the only one who survived to the very end.

00:10:20.040 --> 00:10:24.170
This is the secret ingredient,
a ten-year-old Chateau Lupin.

00:10:27.270 --> 00:10:28.790
Why did you save me?

00:10:28.790 --> 00:10:32.260
You were being so clumsy right in front of me.

00:10:32.260 --> 00:10:34.710
I didn't really intend to, but...

00:10:34.710 --> 00:10:37.800
Maybe because we were almost sent to the other side together?

00:10:38.750 --> 00:10:40.390
I don't like it.

00:10:40.390 --> 00:10:44.310
Don't say that. Eat up!

00:10:44.310 --> 00:10:49.320
Potato gnocchi with a special bolognese ragu sauce.

00:10:50.280 --> 00:10:56.530
The once-unknown fortune teller became suddenly famous in the underworld three years ago.

00:10:57.860 --> 00:11:02.330
A fortune teller who could predict your death day would be popular indeed.

00:11:02.330 --> 00:11:05.330
No, that's not the only reason for his fame.

00:11:05.850 --> 00:11:10.710
All of his clients were people I stole things from before.

00:11:11.110 --> 00:11:14.050
And there's one more interesting person.

00:11:15.890 --> 00:11:18.340
That woman is involved in this, too?

00:11:20.280 --> 00:11:22.130
I don't like it.

00:11:22.130 --> 00:11:24.970
However, I don't want to be indebted to you.

00:11:34.570 --> 00:11:36.530
Aren't <i>you</i> in a good mood?

00:11:37.530 --> 00:11:38.780
Lupin?

00:11:39.250 --> 00:11:41.400
According to Jigen Daisuke,

00:11:41.400 --> 00:11:44.840
you lost a lithograph that you
valued as much as your own life.

00:11:44.840 --> 00:11:47.290
You're looking pretty cheerful despite that.

00:11:47.290 --> 00:11:51.170
I am a fortune teller! Those who come to me

00:11:51.170 --> 00:11:54.410
want to know the day they will die.

00:11:54.410 --> 00:11:58.150
So I tell them the day and receive my payment.

00:11:58.150 --> 00:11:59.300
That is all.

00:11:59.300 --> 00:12:02.430
With a manufactured death day?

00:12:03.250 --> 00:12:04.180
For example,

00:12:04.180 --> 00:12:09.740
using particularly effective hypnotic suggestions when fortunetelling?

00:12:09.740 --> 00:12:14.950
Alternatively, booby-trapping their car or hiring a third-rate assassin.

00:12:14.950 --> 00:12:15.710
Or perhaps...

00:12:16.430 --> 00:12:22.950
Through the use of a capsule like so, you could set the hour, day and year of their death.

00:12:44.750 --> 00:12:46.680
I'm just speculating.

00:12:47.110 --> 00:12:51.060
But there are creatures in this world which live dormant in human guts for years,

00:12:51.060 --> 00:12:53.440
then start expelling strong poisons.

00:12:53.980 --> 00:12:56.530
There are a ridiculous number of ways

00:12:56.570 --> 00:13:00.360
to kill a man a year from now, even if he lives in a bubble of bulletproof glass.

00:13:02.980 --> 00:13:06.200
You don't have the power to see the future at all.

00:13:06.200 --> 00:13:10.210
Mind explaining yourself? Why are you killing people that were involved with me?

00:13:10.920 --> 00:13:12.930
You think you know anything about—

00:13:13.460 --> 00:13:16.500
I don't have any use for guys who don't talk.

00:13:17.140 --> 00:13:19.970
Tell my customers I said, "Hi."

00:13:20.970 --> 00:13:22.220
W-Wait!

00:13:22.220 --> 00:13:25.220
A certain person told me to test you...

00:13:25.220 --> 00:13:28.540
To see if you were a man worthy of their interest...

00:13:28.540 --> 00:13:32.170
To assess if you were a man
suitable for Mine Fujiko or not!

00:13:35.180 --> 00:13:37.440
"A certain person"?

00:13:39.870 --> 00:13:43.090
Well, in any case, you're going to buy back the lithograph, right?

00:13:43.090 --> 00:13:44.200
I'll tag along.

00:14:19.980 --> 00:14:21.680
Wonderful.

00:14:21.680 --> 00:14:24.750
This way, we can show the lithograph to the world.

00:14:24.750 --> 00:14:26.670
You've done well, Mine Fujiko.

00:14:27.090 --> 00:14:28.980
You must be surprised.

00:14:28.980 --> 00:14:32.370
Yes, I am the buyer of this lithograph.

00:14:32.370 --> 00:14:33.600
I can see right through you.

00:14:33.600 --> 00:14:34.190
What?

00:14:34.210 --> 00:14:39.420
Back then, there was a certain someone staring at my butt from the shadow of a pillar.

00:14:46.590 --> 00:14:50.190
Pathetic men always fall for complicated women.

00:14:51.130 --> 00:14:55.000
Before anything else,
you're a cat burglar who lives for money!

00:14:55.000 --> 00:14:58.050
You shouldn't have a problem as long as I pay up, right?

00:14:58.050 --> 00:15:02.380
That's right. I'm just tired of what people expect of me.

00:15:02.380 --> 00:15:05.310
I'm satisfied as long as I get paid.

00:15:05.310 --> 00:15:07.430
Or, that's how it's supposed to be...

00:15:07.430 --> 00:15:08.120
What?

00:15:08.120 --> 00:15:10.390
I charge extra for ogling.

00:15:12.440 --> 00:15:14.030
So it <i>is</i> about money.

00:15:14.030 --> 00:15:19.130
And I'm suddenly interested in the reason you'd put on this over-the-top farce.

00:15:19.860 --> 00:15:22.880
This is something new, Lupin.

00:15:24.090 --> 00:15:29.710
Lately you've been following this fortune teller around quite closely.

00:15:29.710 --> 00:15:31.360
Did you think you had me fooled?

00:15:36.000 --> 00:15:39.100
I felt some connection with this lithograph, you see.

00:15:41.040 --> 00:15:43.610
But I didn't think you would see through me this quickly.

00:15:44.700 --> 00:15:48.380
Well, I'll pay you after I take it back.

00:15:48.380 --> 00:15:50.690
Don't forget about the extra fee.

00:15:55.630 --> 00:15:58.390
"You don't have the ability to see the future at all."

00:15:58.970 --> 00:16:01.500
You said that when we were in the car!

00:16:01.500 --> 00:16:03.630
Why are you so worked up?

00:16:03.630 --> 00:16:07.300
In the past, I really could see the future of my clients,

00:16:07.300 --> 00:16:09.640
and predict their death day!

00:16:09.640 --> 00:16:15.640
But that power gradually weakened and I couldn't read the lithograph any more!

00:16:15.640 --> 00:16:21.150
Whether you believe it or not doesn't matter anymore!

00:16:21.150 --> 00:16:25.870
But I wanted to feel my power again!

00:16:25.870 --> 00:16:26.900
That's when...

00:16:28.280 --> 00:16:31.160
Mine Fujiko, my last job

00:16:31.160 --> 00:16:34.030
is to tell you your death day!

00:16:39.990 --> 00:16:41.050
Me?

00:16:41.690 --> 00:16:43.550
That's interesting and all,

00:16:43.550 --> 00:16:47.060
but didn't you lose your ability to see the future?

00:16:47.060 --> 00:16:50.800
That's <i>if</i> you really had it in the first place.

00:16:51.970 --> 00:16:53.910
You are correct.

00:16:53.910 --> 00:16:56.110
This is my last job.

00:16:56.110 --> 00:16:59.690
With this, I was to be freed of my "fake" ability.

00:17:04.320 --> 00:17:05.570
Don't move, Lupin!

00:17:05.570 --> 00:17:08.820
Drop your guns! You're under arrest!

00:17:08.820 --> 00:17:14.280
Yes, the more people on the stage,
the more interesting it is.

00:17:27.160 --> 00:17:28.550
We're going in!

00:17:30.690 --> 00:17:32.160
An accomplice?!

00:17:32.160 --> 00:17:32.970
Damn!

00:17:37.580 --> 00:17:39.100
I do owe him one,

00:17:39.800 --> 00:17:42.310
but this sure is a boring role to play.

00:17:46.820 --> 00:17:50.430
Don't die, Fujiko. I haven't made love to you yet.

00:17:50.720 --> 00:17:54.090
Until then, you can ask
Zenigata what you're missing out on.

00:17:54.770 --> 00:17:55.910
See you, Lupin.

00:17:56.920 --> 00:17:57.990
Wh-What?!

00:18:13.540 --> 00:18:15.180
This is...

00:18:15.180 --> 00:18:17.430
I know... I know!

00:18:17.890 --> 00:18:18.860
It's back!

00:18:18.860 --> 00:18:20.680
My power has returned!

00:18:20.680 --> 00:18:23.830
I know... I <i>know</i>!

00:18:23.830 --> 00:18:26.190
Mine Fujiko, I'll tell you!

00:18:26.670 --> 00:18:29.690
The day you will die!

00:18:30.690 --> 00:18:37.990
Now is the time to fulfill the final contract with Count Luis Yew Armeid!

00:18:44.840 --> 00:18:45.870
Luis...

00:18:46.320 --> 00:18:47.590
Yew..

00:18:48.320 --> 00:18:50.210
Armeid...

00:19:19.560 --> 00:19:20.450
This can't be...

00:19:21.280 --> 00:19:23.180
Th-This can't be happening!

00:19:23.180 --> 00:19:25.370
Today is my...

00:19:25.370 --> 00:19:26.990
death day.

00:19:44.180 --> 00:19:45.430
What are you doing?

00:19:50.420 --> 00:19:51.650
Stop it!

00:20:11.090 --> 00:20:12.920
It looks like...

00:20:12.920 --> 00:20:17.430
you managed to die just in time for your death day.

00:20:22.470 --> 00:20:24.890
These are photographs taken near the civic hall last night

00:20:24.890 --> 00:20:27.680
at the crime scene where the fortune teller died.

00:20:32.940 --> 00:20:35.440
I knew it was too much for you, kid.

00:20:41.720 --> 00:20:43.170
<i>That bastard.</i>

00:20:44.270 --> 00:20:48.410
<i>He actually died according to his prediction.</i>

00:20:49.900 --> 00:20:51.730
<i>What a conscientious guy.</i>

00:20:53.420 --> 00:20:55.190
<i>However...</i>

00:20:55.190 --> 00:20:56.920
<i>it should be obvious that</i>

00:20:57.290 --> 00:21:00.930
<i>people don't die according to some "death day."</i>

00:21:01.590 --> 00:21:03.800
<i>The day we die</i>

00:21:03.800 --> 00:21:05.930
<i>becomes our death day.</i>

00:21:06.850 --> 00:21:10.940
<i>And nobody decides that for us.</i>

00:21:11.570 --> 00:21:13.050
<i>Don't you agree,</i>

00:21:13.640 --> 00:21:15.270
<i>Mine Fujiko?</i>
